{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8qU4qehprr9oxGXVw6H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ticket 08 is done. A poster job that times out now lets go of everything it took. The full `npm test` passes (4445 tests), lint is clean, and everything is committed except the notes file.\n\nThe fix is in `src/renderer/lib/torrent-poster.js`. Each job keeps a small record of what it holds and whether it has ended. When the job finishes or times out:\n\n1. It removes its server-running subscription.\n2. It sends `wt-stop-server`, but only if it actually sent `wt-start-server`.\n3. Any work still running checks whether the job has ended and stops. A server reply that arrives late asks for no server, and a capture that finishes late writes no poster.\n\n`generateTorrentPoster` takes an optional `{ timeout }` (default still 60 seconds), so the tests in `test/unit/poster.js` give up after 30 ms instead of waiting a minute.\n\nHow each checklist item went:\n\n- [x] A job whose server never answers leaves no server-running subscription once it times out. The test failed before the fix.\n- [x] A job that times out sends `wt-stop-server` for the hold it took. The old code already did this, so I added a test for the other half of the spec: a job that gives up before its subscription is set up asks for no server and releases none, even if the subscription arrives later. That test failed before the fix, and it also caught the old code writing a poster after it had given up.\n- [x] A server reply that arrives after the timeout writes no poster. The tests (one for a late reply, one for a timeout during a capture) fail when I take out the matching checks and pass with them.\n- [x] The next queued job still starts after a timed-out one. This already worked, so the test passed from the start and now guards it.\n\nI also added a short note to `test/AGENTS.md` on passing short timeouts in unit tests. My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, uncommitted.\n\nAs the ticket says, a release sent before the torrent is ready only takes effect with ticket 03's engine change, which is already on this branch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":291,"cache_read_input_tokens":73150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":291},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ce97d0a-4afe-4640-b390-742b9e181571","uuid":"d4ac78a4-5e90-46c7-92da-e96eb71212cf","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:29:43.535Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8qU4bGTWNpBznUsymBy"}
